<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Woodside says reconnecting Cossack.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Woodside says reconnecting Cossack.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woodside Petroleum Ltd said the Cossack Pioneer oil platform offshore of Western Australia was in the process of reconnecting to its mooring and would resume production later on Monday.</p>
<p>The Cossack Pioneer was producing at a rate of about 65,000 barrels a day before disconnecting from its mooring last Thursday as a tropical low off the Western Australia coast threatened to build into a cyclone.</p>
<p>&quot;It's reconnecting as we speak,&quot; a Woodside spokesman told Reuters at 0815 GMT (4.15 p.m.).  </p>
<p>Equal-stake partners in the North West Shelf, where the Cossack Pioneer field is situated, are units of The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd, The British Petroleum Co Plc, Japan Australia LNG (MiMi) Pty Ltd -- a partnership of Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd and Mitsubishi Corp -- Chevron Corp, the Royal Dutch/Shell Group and Woodside.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
